11
00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:14.580
Meanwhile Edward had spent the remainder of the night and morning wandering through the streets of the

12
00:01:14.581 --> 00:01:25.305
city, looking for Miles and thinking hard about what to do next. Somehow he had to stop the

13
00:01:25.306 --> 00:01:31.318
coronation before Tom became king. He stood now among the people in the crowd, who were waiting eagerly

14
00:01:31.319 --> 00:01:37.301
for the king's procession. He was tired, cold, and hungry, and just as eager for this whole sorry

15
00:01:37.302 --> 00:01:48.798
situation to come to an end. Still, he knew he needed a plan. If he confronted Tom

16
00:01:48.799 --> 00:01:56.615
here, the guards would instantly haul him away—and probably toss him back in jail! "If I can somehow

17
00:01:56.616 --> 00:02:06.354
slip into Westminster Abbey ahead of the procession," he thought, "maybe I can hide until Tom and the

18
00:02:06.355 --> 00:02:13.682
